@*
    What a panel shows when its load failed: the sentence PanelBase built ("The board did not
    load.") and the one thing to do about it. One component so every panel says it the same
    way — the Error kind of EmptyState, with the retry as its action — and so no panel is
    tempted to show the exception it caught; that went to the log.

    Shown in place of the panel's body before anything has loaded, and above the rows it
    already holds after, so a refresh that failed does not take numbers the operator was
    reading off the screen.
*@

<EmptyState Kind="EmptyStateKind.Error">
    <ChildContent>@Message</ChildContent>
    <Action>
        <DeskButton Size="DeskKeySize.Small" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Refresh" OnClick="Retry">
            Try again
        </DeskButton>
    </Action>
</EmptyState>

@code {
    /// <summary>The panel's <c>LoadError</c>: a sentence naming what did not load.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string? Message { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The panel's <c>RetryAsync</c>. A callback, so the panel re-renders when it settles.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback OnRetry { get; set; }

    private Task Retry() => OnRetry.InvokeAsync();
}
